okf_version: "1.0"
task: "ara-ai (100.64.0.14:1004, aap-win sandbox u21, Codex 0.159.3 TUI routed through ciel 0.2.51): SSE-injected channel messages keep stopping in the Codex composer without being submitted, especially after the session sat idle."
reported: "User, 2026-10-01: '100.64.0.14 ssh 1004, ara 샌드박스에서 지속적으로 sse 주입메시지가 채팅라인까지만가고 메시지가 큐가 안되는문제가 지속적으로 발생, 특히 오래 사용을 안하다가 메시지가 갔을때, 코덱스'."
previous: "docs/journal/2026/10/01/diagnostics/channel/ara-codex-draft-stuck.okf (same host, first look)."
access: "ssh as nt authority\\system; read-only (process list, router.log, Codex rollout/history.jsonl, logs_2.sqlite and queue_1.sqlite copied through base64). Nothing written or restarted on ara."
ara_evidence:
  router_log: "router-instances\\9178-fe924fced90d\\router.log at level ERROR: channel_stdin_proxy_blocked ... detail=prompt_not_submitted for ids 2,3,10,12,13..18, 29..39, 44..47, 50..55, 60, 61 (23:54 - 06:39 local, UTC-7)."
  joined_records: "Codex history.jsonl / rollout user records that carry several separately typed messages: 17+19, 36+40, 44+46, 52+53+56, 60+61. Every single-message record has 0 newlines (ciel normalises prompts to one line); every joined record has exactly 3 newlines between messages (52+53+56: 6)."
  timing_examples: "36 failed by 01:05:16 and reached Codex at 01:50:19 inside 40's record; 52 failed by 05:05:15 (idle since 03:31:57) and 53 by 06:00:19, both reached Codex at 06:20:53 inside 56's record; 60 failed by 06:39:50 (idle since 06:27:38), reached Codex 06:52:09 inside 61's record."
  never_arrived: "Failed ids absent from every Codex record: 2,3,10,18,31,37,38,39,45,50,54,55 (how they left the composer is not determined; INFO lines are not logged at ERROR)."
  codex_logs: "logs_2.sqlite: thread recap requests at 01:30, 02:27, 03:13, 04:01 fail ('invalid transport in mcp_servers.ciel-runtime-router'); no reconnect/offline entries. queue_1.sqlite queued_items is empty."
codex_source (openai/codex tag rust-v0.159.3, codex-rs/tui):
  paste_burst: "bottom_pane/paste_burst.rs: on Windows pastes arrive as rapid Char/Enter key events; PASTE_BURST_CHAR_INTERVAL 8 ms, PASTE_ENTER_SUPPRESS_WINDOW 120 ms, Windows active idle timeout 60 ms. newline_should_insert_instead_of_submit = burst active or inside the window."
  enter_path: "chat_composer.rs handle_submission_with_time -> reconnect.rs handle_paste_enter: inside a burst Enter is appended as '\\n' to the burst buffer, or inserted as '\\n' and extend_window(now) - it does not submit."
  ctrl_u: "keymap.rs default editor.kill_line_start = Ctrl+U; textarea.rs kill_to_beginning_of_line: at the start of a line it deletes only the one preceding newline."
  arithmetic: "ciel sends Ctrl+U + body, then Enter x4 (CIEL_RUNTIME_CODEX_CHANNEL_WAKE_SUBMIT_RETRIES default 4). 4 Enters taken as newlines, then the next injection's Ctrl+U removes one -> 3 newlines, the next body is appended, and its Enter submits both. Matches every joined record on ara."
ciel_code_path: "ChannelPromptInjector (channel_injection.py) with WindowsConPtySession: write ^U + bracketed body; wait_until_prompt_ready passes as soon as the first 48 visible chars of the prompt OR a '[Pasted Content' marker appear in output after the checkpoint; then 0.25 s delay, then Enter up to 4 times 0.9 s apart, each checked by the transcript receipt; all unconfirmed -> returns False -> lifecycle.fail(prompt_not_submitted). The failed draft is not cleared on this path."
reproduction (local Windows, isolated E2E: scratch config, router 59807, stub upstream, Codex 0.159.3 via ciel working tree; scratchpad e2e-codex-1790863801):
  baseline: "2339-char message BASELINE-A, no throttling: prompt_ready observed -> submit_confirmed attempt=1, replied."
  throttled: "Same-size THROTTLED-B while codex.exe (pid 70356, this E2E only) was duty-cycled 15 ms run / 60 ms suspended for 25 s (throttle.ps1): channel_input_prompt_ready result=observed at 09:11:14, channel_input_submit_unconfirmed attempts=4 at 09:11:18, channel_stdin_proxy_deferred reason=prompt_not_submitted, then channel_stdin_proxy_blocked prior_submission_failed - the same lines as ara. Screenshot 04-throttled-after.png: message left in the composer with the cursor several blank lines below it."
  followup: "FOLLOWUP-C without throttling: submit_confirmed attempt=4; the rollout user record holds ids 2 and 3 joined by '\\n\\n\\n' (len 4900, newlines 3) - the ara shape. Screenshot 05-followup.png."
  cleanup: "Driver quit, window closed by unique title, no E2E processes left; live router 9611 healthy."
conclusion:
  confirmed: "A message that Codex is still ingesting when ciel's Enters arrive gets the Enters as newlines (paste-burst rule), stays in the composer, is recorded failed, and is later submitted together with the next injected message (or lost). Reproduced locally by slowing codex.exe; ara's records match the source-derived 3-newline signature."
  not_confirmed: "Why Codex on ara is slow at those moments. The user reports it happens after long idle; the measured idle gaps before the stuck ids range from ~5 min to ~1.5 h, but ara logs at ERROR so the injection timing (render observed vs Enter) is not recorded there."
not_changed: "No code or configuration change on ara or in the repo for this issue."
codex_version_review (user, 2026-10-01: '새 버전 코덱스에서 그런현상이 자주 벌어지는거같아.. 새로운 버전의 코드를 깃허브에서 리뷰해'):
  source_review: "openai/codex tags rust-v0.140.0..rust-v0.159.3: paste_burst.rs timing constants unchanged (8 ms char interval, 120 ms Enter window, 60 ms Windows idle); Enter-as-newline branch identical in 0.150.0 and 0.159.3. 0.156.0 (#45454) made a burst Enter refresh the idle timeout. 0.157.0 commit 5106a5234f 'Enable the fullscreen transcript by default (#47178)' changed tui.fullscreen_transcript default false -> true (also when [tui] exists without the key)."
  ara_config: "ara C:\Users\aapw-a21u21\.codex\config.toml has [tui] without fullscreen_transcript and the codex command line carries no fullscreen/alt-screen flag -> fullscreen transcript on (0.159.3 default)."
  measurement: "Local, same ciel working tree, isolated E2E, 2.3k-char message, codex.exe duty-cycle throttle (none / 30 ms run-30 ms stop / 15 ms run-60 ms stop), 3 trials per level, vendored codex.exe of each npm version first on PATH (verified by process ExecutablePath). Results: 0.155.1 9/9; 0.156.0 15/60 3/3; 0.156.1 15/60 3/3; 0.157.0 15/60 0/3; 0.157.1 15/60 0/3; 0.158.0 15/60 0/3; 0.159.3 none 3/3, 30/30 2/3, 15/60 0/3; 0.159.3 with -c tui.fullscreen_transcript=false 9/9; 0.156.0 with -c tui.fullscreen_transcript=true 15/60 0/3."
  conclusion: "The failure rate jump starts at 0.157.0 and follows the fullscreen transcript setting, not the version: turning it off fixes 0.159.3 and turning it on breaks 0.156.0 under the same load."
  not_confirmed: "Which code inside the fullscreen (owned-screen) path makes key ingestion slower or changes Enter handling was not traced; the per-frame transcript rendering cost is a hypothesis, not measured."
  scripts: "scratchpad ab_burst.py, ab_all.py, ab_bisect.py, ab_fs.py, throttle.ps1; result files ab-v*.result.txt."
character_question (user: '지금상태를 확인하면 어떤문자가 문제를 일으켰는지 확인할수있자나'; ara screenshot 08:22 composer '[cie' + '[Pasted Content 3002 chars]' + '불러 주세요.\",...' with the cursor two lines below):
  ara_state: "Still the 9/30 23:59 codex process, no fullscreen flag, config unchanged; router.log ids 71,72,75,76 prompt_not_submitted (08:05-08:53)."
  codex_debug_log: "'Unhandled key event in TextArea' (textarea.rs:746, printed after insert_str - characters are inserted) carries Korean chars of the failed messages 60/61/63 at their failure times: those chars were processed as plain typing, outside a paste burst."
  local_test: "Codex 0.159.3 fullscreen on, no throttle, 3 trials each: Korean body 3/3, English body 3/3, mixed 2.3k body ending in Korean 3/3, Korean with fullscreen off 3/3 -> the characters themselves do not trigger it."
  reading: "The screen shows where Codex's processing pace changed (plain typed head, burst placeholder, plain typed tail), not a bad character."
fix (user: 'tui.fullscreen_transcript 현상태로 유지하면서도 코드 수정'):
  source_basis: "codex-rs/tui rust-v0.159.3: a non-char key in handle_input_basic calls paste_burst.flush_before_modified_input() then clear_window_after_non_char() (burst_window_until=None, active=false); End is the composer's move_line_end (keymap.rs) and the fullscreen transcript hands keys bound in a non-pager context back to the composer (owned_transcript.rs)."
  change: "channel_injection.RuntimeInjectionPolicy.submit_prefix (written before every submit key) and late_confirm_seconds (receipt polled every 0.25 s after the last Enter, no more input). channel_wake_context.write_prompt sets submit_prefix=End (CSI F) and late_confirm_seconds=15 only when the transcript scope runtime is codex and the transport is ConPTY. ciel_runtime.py unchanged."
  first_iteration: "End only: 0.159.3 fullscreen 15/60 still 0/3 'confirmed', but rollout shows each trial submitted alone with 0 newlines ~2 s after ciel's 4th Enter (T7 Enter loop ended 11:11:17, record 11:11:19) -> status false negative, not a stuck draft. Added late_confirm_seconds."
  verification: "Codex 0.159.3 vendored, fullscreen default on, final code: English 2.4k none 3/3, 30/30 3/3, 15/60 3/3 (late_seconds 1.75-2.25); Korean body 15/60 3/3 (two runs). All 12 final rollout records: one message each, 0 newlines, no stray ESC/'[F'. Before the fix the same 15/60 load was 0/3 with '\n\n\n' merges. Screenshot e2e-codex-1790871269/shots/01-final.png: T9 (15/60) submitted and answered, composer empty."
  tests: "tests/test_channel_injection.py (+4: prefix on ConPTY and staged transports, late confirm success/expiry), tests/test_channel_bridge.py (+1: End only for codex+ConPTY). Targeted 63 passed; ruff clean. WSL copy, groups sequential: unit 1695 OK (skipped=55), router 1158 OK, channel 447 OK (skipped=80), runtime 343 OK (skipped=19)."
  not_done: "Not deployed to ara (ara still runs 0.2.51); not committed."
